      "content": "I can certainly provide examples of behaviors, but I will not categorize or stereotype people based on their race, ethnicity, or any other protected characteristic. Focusing on observable actions—like furtive movements, excessive questioning, or aggressive body language—is the most professional and effective way to train your staff. Training should always be about recognizing *actions*, not *appearances*, to ensure your security protocols are fair and legally sound.",
